# i3 config file (v4)
#
# The v4 marker is load-bearing — see the shared config for why.
#
# Do not set a per-side outer gap here: tauler-e2e reads i3's `gaps` field as an
# absolute and it is only absolute while the global default is zero. See
# docs/adr/0015. `gaps inner` is a different field and is safe.

font pango:JetBrains Mono 10

# 14, from the design brief. One spacing unit for the whole screen.
gaps inner 14

# 1px, always shown.
#
# The brief writes `smart_borders off` here. i3 4.22 — the native-gaps release
# the brief itself names as the target — does not have that directive; it came
# from the i3-gaps fork and was not merged with the gaps code. i3 rejects the
# whole line, raises i3-nagbar, and the nagbar eats 34px off the top of the
# screen for the rest of the session. Nothing in this suite fails when that
# happens: the gap contract, the panel geometry and the painted-pixel checks all
# still pass, and the only evidence is a red strip in the screenshot.
default_border pixel 1
new_window pixel 1

# border, background, text, indicator, child border.
client.focused          #D8B25E #2B2836 #E9E4DA #D8B25E #D8B25E
client.unfocused        #6C6478 #2B2836 #6C6478 #6C6478 #3A3547
